A||||4||BN Boomer||Has anybody retrofitted sail panel speakers into an 84-85 Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||BN Boomer||05-03-2000||09:33 PM||||Well, the title pretty much says it all. I've been thinking about trying to put sail panel speakers into my 85 GT as one way to help improve the stereo system. Has anyone else done this? Could I have I both sail panel speakers and the headrest speakers operative? I know I would need new interior pieces with the speaker cutouts and covers and I may be able to use the speaker mounting plates and wiring harness out of my 87 Coupe parts car.<P>Also, I've been looking at a Pioneer DEH-P86DHR stereo system. Crutchfield's currently has it for $299 with a free direct connect wire harness and steering wheel mounted remote control (not sure if I really care about that). Any opinions on this unit?||||reg||5
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||05-03-2000||11:28 PM||||   Boomer,<BR>  Getting ready to do the same thing to my 85GT. This weekend I'm off to a wrecking yard<BR>to get the rear window(w/defroster)and dark grey interior panels, which happen to have the sail panel speakers. I'm sure it can be done with a little patience. Let me know,or, I'll let you know. <P>  Be Cool <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Hock||05-04-2000||04:37 AM||||YES IT CAN BE DONE. BESURE TO LOOK AT THE 87 YOUR USING FOR PARTS AND MAKE SURE IF YOU HAVE TO CUT OR NOT.<P>I WOULD ALSO SUGGEST GOING WITH AN AFTERMARKET RADIO SO YOU GET THE SOUND YOU WANT.<P>GOOD LUCK!!!!!!! ||||reg||14
Z||000003||BN Boomer||05-04-2000||09:24 AM||||Hey, I happen to have the grey interior panels with speaker cutouts and covers out of my 87 Coupe. Unfortunately, I need the saddle colored ones for my 85 GT.||||reg||7
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-04-2000||10:10 AM||||I was gonna do that to the Grape Ape until I removed the sail panels and realized that there aren't any holes for the speakers to sit in.  I don't mind getting the Dremel out, but I don't want to go through the hassle.  You'll have to cut just the right size holes, then probably drill and tap screw/bolt holes.  Looked like a real pain in the @$$.  I think I'll just go with a set of 5 1/4" separates instead.  That or I could just transfer everything to the Monkeymobile frame.  Probably not.||||reg||1
